course: dictionary
lesson: 10946
title: Wail: a long, loud cry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To wail is to cry out with a long, loud, high sound because of pain, sadness or anger. It is not a quick shout. It is a sound that goes on and on.
explain: Wail can describe a sound that is not a person. «A faint "Poop-poop!" wailed like an uneasy animal in pain.» A horn can wail, so the word tells you the sound is long, high and sad or uneasy.
explain: The wind and sirens can wail too. Look at the words around wail: they tell you whether it is a person crying or a sound in the air.
fact: Wail means a long, loud, high cry or sound.
fact: A wail (noun) is one of those long cries: let out a wail.
fact: Wail is a verb too: wail, wails, wailed, wailing.
fact: «"Poop-poop!" wailed like an uneasy animal in pain.» Here wailed describes a sound, not a person.
fact: Other phrases: wail with grief, the wail of a siren.
exercise: What does wail mean? | To run very fast | To laugh quietly | To whisper a secret | *To cry out with a long, loud, high sound
exercise: Find and copy the verb in this sentence: «A faint "Poop-poop!" wailed like an uneasy animal in pain.» | uneasy | *wailed | faint | animal
exercise: The wind began to wail outside the window. What is wailing here? | *The wind, making a long, high sound | A dog sleeping | A child laughing | A bird singing sweetly
test: In the phrase «the wail of a siren», what kind of word is wail? | A noun meaning a soft whisper | An adjective meaning bright | A verb meaning to laugh | *A noun meaning a long, loud, high sound
test: Someone says «She wailed with grief when she heard the news.» Which words best match wailed? | Ran quickly away | *Cried out loudly in sadness | Sang softly to herself | Giggled and clapped
exam: Which best describes a wail? | A quiet hum, like a bee | A bright light in the sky | A sudden giggle | *A long, loud, high cry of pain, sadness or anger
